    "updated_at": "2025-03-24T16:44:27Z",
    "body": "I looked at https://github.com/whatwg/urlpattern/pull/255 and https://github.com/whatwg/urlpattern/issues/220.\n\nBasically we'll have a dummy URL with a special scheme, but what if a non-special scheme is specified? e.g. `{protocol: 'git', hostname: 'café.com'}`? In that case the encoded string should be `caf%C3%A9.com`, rather than `xn--caf-dma.com`? If so, I feel https://github.com/whatwg/urlpattern/pull/255 is a reasonable approach.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
